18:["$","h2","3",{"className":"mt-12 t-h3 text-ink","children":"Step 1: Get the idea out of your head"}]
19:["$","p","4",{"className":"mt-5 text-lg leading-[1.75] text-ink","children":"Open Claude Code, turn voice mode on, and explain your entire app idea in as much detail as you can. Who it's for, what it does, what every screen looks like, and why someone would pick it over what already exists. Talking gets a lot more detail out of you than typing does."}]
1a:["$","p","5",{"className":"mt-5 text-lg leading-[1.75] text-ink","children":"When you're done talking, paste this:"}]
1b:["$","div","6",{"className":"mt-5","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"mb-2 flex items-center justify-between gap-4","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-mono text-[12px] text-ink-dim","children":"PRD and CLAUDE.md"}],["$","$L3b",null,{"text":"That's my whole app idea. Before you write anything, ask me every question you need answered to build it.\n\nThen write two files:\n1. PRD.md: a concise product requirements doc. What the app does, who it's for, the core features for v1, what's out of scope, and how we'll know it works.\n2. CLAUDE.md: the project summary, the stack, the commands, and the always and never rules you'll follow every session. Tell yourself to read PRD.md before starting any work."}]]}],["$","pre",null,{"className":"rounded-xl bg-[#0a1020] p-5 font-mono text-[13px] leading-[1.7] text-[#e4e9f5] whitespace-pre-wrap break-words","children":["$","code",null,{"children":"That's my whole app idea. Before you write anything, ask me every question you need answered to build it.\n\nThen write two files:\n1. PRD.md: a concise product requirements doc. What the app does, who it's for, the core features for v1, what's out of scope, and how we'll know it works.\n2. CLAUDE.md: the project summary, the stack, the commands, and the always and never rules you'll follow every session. Tell yourself to read PRD.md before starting any work."}]}]]}]
1c:["$","p","7",{"className":"mt-5 text-lg leading-[1.75] text-ink","children":"Make a new folder for the project and put both files in it. Everything after this runs on those two files. If you want Claude to remember where it left off between sessions too, add the other three docs from this guide:"}]
1d:["$","ul","8",{"className":"mt-5 divide-y divide-line border-y border-line","children":[["$","li","/vault/vibe-coding-docs",{"children":["$","a",null,{"href":"/vault/vibe-coding-docs","className":"group flex items-start gap-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"min-w-0 flex-1","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"block font-semibold text-ink transition-colors group-hover:text-accent","children":"4 docs that keep your AI coding agent from losing the plot"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-0.5 block text-[15px] leading-[1.6] text-ink-soft","children":"CLAUDE.md, progress.md, known-issues.md and decisions.md, with templates."}]]}],["$","span",null,{"aria-hidden":true,"className":"mt-0.5 text-ink-dim transition-colors group-hover:text-accent","children":"→"}]]}]}]]}]
1e:["$","h2","9",{"className":"mt-12 t-h3 text-ink","children":"Step 2: Plan the whole build"}]
1f:["$","p","10",{"className":"mt-5 text-lg leading-[1.75] text-ink","children":"Switch to the best model you have with /model, then type /plan (or press Shift+Tab until it says plan mode) and paste this. The plan decides how the rest of the build goes, so this is where the smartest model is worth it."}]
20:["$","div","11",{"className":"mt-5","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"mb-2 flex items-center justify-between gap-4","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-mono text-[12px] text-ink-dim","children":"The plan"}],["$","$L3b",null,{"text":"Plan the entire build of this app from PRD.md and CLAUDE.md. Break it into phases small enough to build and test one at a time. For each phase, list the files it touches, what done looks like, and how you'll test it. Flag anything in the PRD that's unclear or risky. Don't write any code until I approve the plan."}]]}],["$","pre",null,{"className":"rounded-xl bg-[#0a1020] p-5 font-mono text-[13px] leading-[1.7] text-[#e4e9f5] whitespace-pre-wrap break-words","children":["$","code",null,{"children":"Plan the entire build of this app from PRD.md and CLAUDE.md. Break it into phases small enough to build and test one at a time. For each phase, list the files it touches, what done looks like, and how you'll test it. Flag anything in the PRD that's unclear or risky. Don't write any code until I approve the plan."}]}]]}]
21:["$","p","12",{"className":"mt-5 text-lg leading-[1.75] text-ink","children":"Actually read the plan before you approve it. If a phase looks too big, tell it to split that phase in two. If it picked a tool you don't want, say so now. Swapping a tool out halfway through the build is a lot more work."}]
22:["$","h2","13",{"className":"mt-12 t-h3 text-ink","children":"Step 3: Build it in a loop"}]
23:["$","p","14",{"className":"mt-5 text-lg leading-[1.75] text-ink","children":"Now start coding with loop engineering. Claude builds one phase, checks its own work, fixes whatever broke, and only moves on once it passes. That stops it from stacking ten features on top of a bug it never noticed."}]
24:["$","div","15",{"className":"mt-5","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"mb-2 flex items-center justify-between gap-4","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-mono text-[12px] text-ink-dim","children":"The build loop"}],["$","$L3b",null,{"text":"Build the next phase of the plan. When you think it's done, check your own work: run the app, run the tests, and compare the result against what done looks like for this phase. If anything fails, fix it and check again. Keep looping until it all passes, then tell me exactly what you checked and what's left."}]]}],["$","pre",null,{"className":"rounded-xl bg-[#0a1020] p-5 font-mono text-[13px] leading-[1.7] text-[#e4e9f5] whitespace-pre-wrap break-words","children":["$","code",null,{"children":"Build the next phase of the plan. When you think it's done, check your own work: run the app, run the tests, and compare the result against what done looks like for this phase. If anything fails, fix it and check again. Keep looping until it all passes, then tell me exactly what you checked and what's left."}]}]]}]
25:["$","ul","16",{"className":"mt-5 space-y-3","children":[["$","li","0",{"className":"flex gap-3 leading-[1.7] text-ink","children":[["$","span",null,{"aria-hidden":true,"className":"mt-2.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-accent"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Paste it once per phase until the whole plan is done."}]]}],["$","li","1",{"className":"flex gap-3 leading-[1.7] text-ink","children":[["$","span",null,{"aria-hidden":true,"className":"mt-2.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-accent"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Start each phase in a fresh session with /clear, so the model isn't dragging the last phase around in its memory."}]]}],["$","li","2",{"className":"flex gap-3 leading-[1.7] text-ink","children":[["$","span",null,{"aria-hidden":true,"className":"mt-2.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-accent"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Actually open the app and click around after every phase. Tests passing doesn't mean it works the way you pictured it."}]]}],["$","li","3",{"className":"flex gap-3 leading-[1.7] text-ink","children":[["$","span",null,{"aria-hidden":true,"className":"mt-2.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-accent"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Commit to GitHub after every phase that passes, so you can always roll back to the last version that worked."}]]}]]}]
26:["$","h2","17",{"className":"mt-12 t-h3 text-ink","children":"Step 4: Audit it so you don't get hacked or sued"}]
27:["$","p","18",{"className":"mt-5 text-lg leading-[1.75] text-ink","children":"Once it's done building, we need to work on security. The first prompt hunts for the holes that get you hacked. The second hunts for the things that get you sued or taken down. Run them one at a time and fix every CRITICAL before you touch anything else."}]
3c:T413,Audit this codebase like someone trying to hack it. Check every item below. For each one: PASS, FAIL, or CAN'T TELL. For every FAIL, cite the file and line, rate it CRITICAL, HIGH, or LOW, and give me the fix. Report first. Don't change anything yet.

HACKED
1. Secrets: hardcoded keys, a committed .env, keys in git history or the frontend bundle
2. Auth: routes with no session check, permission checks only in the frontend, user IDs trusted from the request, tokens in localStorage, no email verification or password rules
3. Database: tables with RLS off, policies that let user A read user B's rows, IDs with no ownership check, updates that save the whole request body
4. Input: SQL built from strings, user content rendered as raw HTML, no server-side validation, unchecked file uploads
5. Exposure: no rate limits on login or AI routes, unsigned webhooks, CORS set to *, open /admin or debug routes, stack traces in production, outdated dependencies

Then rank the fails by how likely each one is to hurt me, and give me the fix order.3d:T413,Audit this codebase like someone trying to hack it. Check every item below. For each one: PASS, FAIL, or CAN'T TELL. For every FAIL, cite the file and line, rate it CRITICAL, HIGH, or LOW, and give me the fix. Report first. Don't change anything yet.

HACKED
1. Secrets: hardcoded keys, a committed .env, keys in git history or the frontend bundle
2. Auth: routes with no session check, permission checks only in the frontend, user IDs trusted from the request, tokens in localStorage, no email verification or password rules
3. Database: tables with RLS off, policies that let user A read user B's rows, IDs with no ownership check, updates that save the whole request body
4. Input: SQL built from strings, user content rendered as raw HTML, no server-side validation, unchecked file uploads
5. Exposure: no rate limits on login or AI routes, unsigned webhooks, CORS set to *, open /admin or debug routes, stack traces in production, outdated dependencies

